// A stub dependency runtime that this fixture's probe recipe genuinely *runs*.
//
// Unlike the `primitive-consumer/` stub next door — never executed, present so
// the bare import can be planned as an accepted dependency edge — this one is
// copied into the private probe workspace as part of the authenticated
// dependency closure and called from inside a launched worker. Its answer is
// the recipe's evidence that the specifier resolved to authenticated bytes:
// the recipe refuses the gate on any other value.
//
// It defines no Solid primitive on purpose. `record` is not a name in either
// dialect's vocabulary, so nothing here can be mistaken for a dialect axiom or
// drag the census's dialect tier into a fixture about module resolution.
export function record(value) {
  return `recorded:${value}`;
}
